# Dockerfile.pi-planner — pi-contracts:latest + pi-subagents, for the
# planner role (the host project's launch-planner.sh).
#
# Kept SEPARATE from Dockerfile.pi-contracts (the worker's image), same
# reasoning as Dockerfile.pi-integrator: pi-subagents' BACKGROUND/detached-
# runner children are an unverified tool_call-routing path - unconfirmed
# whether that detached process inherits --extension/CONTRACT_GUARDS, so a
# background child could in principle bypass contract-guard entirely. That
# risk matters far more for a worker (owned_paths is the only fence standing
# between it and the rest of the repo) than for the planner, which is
# already docs-only fenced to docs/changes/**, docs/decisions/** regardless
# of which agent or sub-agent makes the write - a bypassed background child
# still can't reach application code through this guard. Prefer FOREGROUND
# sub-agent delegation until the background case is verified empirically
# (see docs/changes/COORDINATION.md "Grounding a weak mission").
#
# Used for the research phase of grounding a weak mission: one sub-agent per
# candidate direction/mission, researched in parallel, each producing its own
# cited note under docs/changes/_research/ before any boundary gets drafted.
#
#   ./build.sh planner   (or: ./build.sh ensure all)
# The base is passed in by build.sh (--build-arg BASE_IMAGE=<slug>-pi-contracts:latest),
# derived from contracts/.harness-slug - never hard-code a namespaced name here.
ARG BASE_IMAGE=pi-contracts:latest
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

USER node
RUN pi install npm:pi-subagents
RUN pi install npm:pi-hashline-edit-pro
